:"text_result","domain":"spec.commonmark.org","ref_id":"turn0search11","snippet":"A link reference definition consists of a link label, indented up to three spaces, followed by a colon (`:`), optional whitespace (including up to one","title":"CommonMark Spec","url":"https://spec.commonmark.org/0.25/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"commonmark-ja.readthedocs.io","ref_id":"turn0search12","snippet":"CommonMark ... <visual_element id=\"e2\"> ... A [link reference definition] consists of a [link label], indented up to three spaces, followed by a colon (:), optional","title":"CommonMark","url":"https://commonmark-ja.readthedocs.io/_/downloads/ja/latest/pdf/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"de.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn0search13","snippet":"Aktuelle Version | 0.31.2 ... http://commonmark.org/","title":"CommonMark","url":"https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/CommonMark"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.reddit.com","ref_id":"turn0reddit14","snippet":"[Thursday September 12 2019] [+0 votes] ... Check whether the first line matches the \"full\" reference definition. i.e. check whether label, url and optionally a","title":"I need help with creating regex that can verify Markdown link reference","url":"https://www.reddit.com/r/regex/comments/d39hv4"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn0search15","snippet":"0.31.2 ... Type of format | Open file format ... Website | commonmark.org spec.commonmark.org","title":"Markdown","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Markdown"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn0search16","snippet":"A newline (frequently called line ending, end of line (EOL), next line (NEL) or line break) is a control character or sequence of control characters","title":"Newline","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newline"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"pt.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn0search17","snippet":"* «CommonMark Spec 0.31.2». 28 de janeiro de 2024. ... * Steele, Shawn (24 de abril de 1996). «cp437_DOSLatinUS to Unicode table, version 2.00».","title":"Ponto lista","url":"https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ponto_lista"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn0search18","snippet":"Most LMLs follow one of two styles for headings, either Setext-like underlines or atx-like line markers, or they support both. ... Reference syntax ... Org-mode's","title":"Lightweight markup language","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lightweight_markup_language"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn0search19","snippet":"Two common void elements are <br /> (for a hard line-break, such as in a poem or an address) and <hr /> (for a thematic","title":"HTML element","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTML_element"}]}}
