{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'git diff 8e3009b2c7305cd94500009875ddc1b7880d8331 32417974a9cfd5392fabbd8d0ad50305e43ce99f -- pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/spec.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go .pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md'","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/.pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md b/.pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md\nindex 6e369a55..570b9503 100644\n--- a/.pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md\n+++ b/.pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md\n@@ -229,3 +229,24 @@ uses Read/Grep/Glob/Bash without Edit/Write/Agent tools or plan approval mode.\n This changes neither independence nor stream/output/run limits; the actual\n working tree remains checked for mutation. No vendor profile becomes a scaffold\n default.\n+\n+\n+## Capacity recalibration of captured input bytes (D10) — 2026-11-13\n+\n+Closing spec `pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit`, `pose index` in a\n+fresh clone and then in the maintainer checkout refused the pose-dist corpus:\n+`index.delivery-integrity` exceeded the captured-input budget and\n+`index.generate` was left without a complete observation. Measured with a Git\n+shim on the real builder: the change sets of every spec read `git show\n+--binary` for 2,451 distinct trailer commits, 492 MB of Git output in the\n+capture (the final audit reads it again under its own budget), plus the file\n+inputs of the generation, so the operation needed more than 512 MiB. Nothing\n+was truncated; the refusal was correct. Raise the captured-input budget to\n+1 GiB, for capture and audit alike, and keep every other limit, including the\n+512 MiB executable-hash bound of D9. Observations retain their bytes, so the\n+operation may now hold up to 1 GiB of captured input in memory. This\n+recalibration buys headroom, not a scaling property: the corpus grows with\n+every attributed commit. The structural fix, retaining only a digest for pure\n+reads of immutable Git objects whose bytes a producer only hashes, is a\n+follow-up of that spec, and a further raise again requires a measured\n+reassessment.\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go\nindex 5d9f6e5d..1072fd11 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go\n@@ -22,12 +22,17 @@ const (\n \tGovernanceReadViewSchemaVersion = 1\n \tgovernanceReadViewParserVersion = \"pose-governance-inputs-v1\"\n \tgovernanceReadViewMaxRecords    = 40000\n-\tgovernanceReadViewMaxInputBytes = 512 * 1024 * 1024\n+\tgovernanceReadViewMaxInputBytes = 1024 * 1024 * 1024\n \tgovernanceReadViewMaxMetadata   = 16 * 1024 * 1024\n \tReadViewFreshnessCurrent        = \"current\"\n \tReadViewFreshnessUnknown        = \"unknown\"\n )\n \n+// GovernanceReadViewMaxInputBytes is the captured-input budget of one\n+// governance read view, capture and audit alike (ADR\n+// governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views, D10).\n+const GovernanceReadViewMaxInputBytes = governanceReadViewMaxInputBytes\n+\n var errGovernanceReadViewWrite = errors.New(\"pose: governance read view is read-only\")\n var errGovernanceReadViewFinalized = errors.New(\"pose: governance read view is finalized\")\n var errGovernanceReadViewOutsideRoot = errors.New(\"pose: governance read view input escapes the project root\")\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go\nindex 0782e239..7182af75 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go\n@@ -131,6 +131,10 @@ type ReviewPlan struct {\n \tWarnings                  []string `json:\"warnings,omitempty\"`\n \tBlockers                  []string `json:\"blockers,omitempty\"`\n \tExplain                   []string `json:\"explain\"`\n+\t// CloseoutReview is the closeout-review@1 decision for a milestone or a\n+\t// roadmap under an adopted policy. Like Band it is a projection: it stays\n+\t// out of the plan digest (spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit).\n+\tCloseoutReview *CloseoutReviewDecision `json:\"closeout_review,omitempty\"`\n }\n \n type reviewRepoEntry struct {\n@@ -397,6 +401,16 @@ func (s Store) ReviewPlan(ref string) (ReviewPlan, error) {\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn ReviewPlan{}, err\n \t}\n+\t// Warnings and Explain enter the digest; the decision does not, so it is\n+\t// attached only as its own field. A gate that cannot answer (a corrupt or\n+\t// drifted receipt) fails the plan as it fails closeout-check.\n+\tif !s.planWithoutCloseoutGate {\n+\t\tdecision, _, gateErr := s.closeoutReviewGate(ref, policy)\n+\t\tif gateErr != nil {\n+\t\t\treturn ReviewPlan{}, gateErr\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tplan.CloseoutReview = decision\n+\t}\n \treturn plan, nil\n }\n \n@@ -565,7 +579,7 @@ func (s Store) reviewScopeSpecs(scope ScopeRef) ([]Spec, error) {\n \t\t// Another project's member contributes no local components; its\n \t\t// review lives in its own project and reaches this scope through the\n \t\t// federated manifest.\n-\t\tslug, external := s.milestoneMember(raw)\n+\t\tslug, external := s.canonicalMember(raw)\n \t\tif external {\n \t\t\tcontinue\n \t\t}\n@@ -1085,6 +1099,7 @@ func (s Store) addMilestoneGateCriterion(scope ScopeRef, criteria []ReviewPlanCr\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn criteria, blockers\n \t}\n+\tadopted, _ := s.closeoutReviewPolicyAdopted()\n \tfor _, rm := range roadmaps {\n \t\tif terminalStatuses[rm.Status] {\n \t\t\tcontinue\n@@ -1094,10 +1109,19 @@ func (s Store) addMilestoneGateCriterion(scope ScopeRef, criteria []ReviewPlanCr\n \t\t\t\tcontinue\n \t\t\t}\n \t\t\tref := ScopeRef{Kind: \"milestone\", Roadmap: rm.Slug, Milestone: milestone.ID}\n-\t\t\tif member, ok := s.soleMemberOf(ref); !ok || member != scope.Slug {\n+\t\t\tmember, ok := s.soleMemberOf(ref)\n+\t\t\tcarries := ok && member == scope.Slug\n+\t\t\t// Under an adopted closeout review policy a milestone of more\n+\t\t\t// members may close without its own review; its gate is then\n+\t\t\t// judged in the review of its last member (spec\n+\t\t\t// pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit, review round 5 N19).\n+\t\t\tif !carries && adopted {\n+\t\t\t\tcarries = s.lastOpenMemberOf(rm.Slug, milestone, scope.Slug)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tif !carries {\n \t\t\t\tcontinue\n \t\t\t}\n-\t\t\tif done && !sealedCarries(\"milestone-exit-gate-\"+rm.Slug+\"-\"+milestone.ID) {\n+\t\t\tif done && !sealedCarries(milestoneExitGateCriterionID(rm.Slug, milestone.ID)) {\n \t\t\t\tif historyUnknown != \"\" {\n \t\t\t\t\t// Absent history is not unreadable history: the plan says it cannot\n \t\t\t\t\t// tell whether the gate was sealed, instead of silently dropping it.\n@@ -1106,8 +1130,8 @@ func (s Store) addMilestoneGateCriterion(scope ScopeRef, criteria []ReviewPlanCr\n \t\t\t\tcontinue\n \t\t\t}\n \t\t\tcriteria, blockers = addReviewCriterion(criteria, ReviewPlanCriterion{\n-\t\t\t\tID:          \"milestone-exit-gate-\" + rm.Slug + \"-\" + milestone.ID,\n-\t\t\t\tDescription: \"The exit gate of milestone:\" + rm.Slug + \"/\" + milestone.ID + \" holds: \" + milestone.ExitGate,\n+\t\t\t\tID:          milestoneExitGateCriterionID(rm.Slug, milestone.ID),\n+\t\t\t\tDescription: milestoneExitGateCriterionDescription(rm.Slug, milestone.ID, milestone.ExitGate),\n \t\t\t\tRequired:    true,\n \t\t\t\tKind:        ReviewCriterionKindJudgment,\n \t\t\t\tProfiles:    []string{\"milestone-exit-gate\"},\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/spec.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/spec.go\nindex bd17f7a4..aada4858 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/spec.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/spec.go\n@@ -56,6 +56,10 @@ type Store struct {\n \tRoot               string // project root containing .pose/\n \tFederatedProjectID string\n \tFederatedResolver  *ArtifactResolver\n+\t// closeoutChain is the chain of local aggregate scopes whose terminal\n+\t// verification is asking for this one, through their dependency edges:\n+\t// a scope already in it is a cycle and is not proven closed.\n+\tcloseoutChain []string\n \t// specs, when set, is the spec listing of one operation, read once\n \t// (spec pose-attention-within-a-second). Nil outside such an operation.\n \tspecs *specSnapshot\n@@ -67,6 +71,10 @@ type Store struct {\n \t// the disk, a preview reads its staged view. A store built from this one\n \t// carries it on.\n \tFS Files\n+\t// planWithoutCloseoutGate builds a review plan without asking the\n+\t// closeout review gate, for the gate's own question about the plan's\n+\t// effective independence (spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit).\n+\tplanWithoutCloseoutGate bool\n }\n \n // fsys is the store's filesystem.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
