{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_85","type":"agent_message","text":"The sweep is complete. I found three medium blockers: missed reference definitions, missed angle-bracket links containing an escaped `>`, and incorrect decoding of backslash-escaped character references. Each can suppress a real ADR association and grant an exemption. N48 is therefore partially fixed. N49’s conservative over-enforcement remains a low follow-up. The repository is unchanged, and `go vet ./...` passed."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_86","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nThree medium blockers remain in ADR association parsing:\n\n- **N50, line 37:** valid reference definitions with multiline labels, escaped brackets, or blockquote prefixes disappear silently.\n- **N51, line 35:** valid angle-bracket links containing an escaped `>` can disappear silently.\n- **N52, line 56:** entity decoding incorrectly interprets backslash-escaped character references.\n\nEach can grant an incorrect `when-justified` exemption. Read-only probes compared the extracted production expressions with CommonMark rendering. These forms are supported by the [CommonMark specification](https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/#links).\n\nThe closeout-policy tests passed across domain, CLI, and MCP packages; `go vet ./...` passed. Surface-check reported zero findings. The exact artifact-check exited 0, with provenance warnings and an older recorded change set; an additional explicit-range invocation failed with `signal: broken pipe`.\n\nRules applied: backend-go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence under the review workflow. No repository changes or attestation were made.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N50\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\",\n      \"line\": 37,\n      \"summary\": \"Recognize valid reference definitions or report them as unknown. The expression excludes multiline labels and escaped closing brackets, and its line anchor excludes definitions inside blockquotes. Read-only probes using the extracted production expressions returned no destinations for '[decision][decision label]\\\\n\\\\n[decision\\\\nlabel]: ../adr/decision.md', '[decision][d]\\\\n\\\\n> [d]: ../adr/decision.md', and an escaped-bracket label; CommonMark rendering resolves each to decision.md. Equivalent backlinks to pair.md also disappear. Because no match reaches add(), no diagnostic is produced. With two canonical members and no other association, the evaluator returns Known=true and Required=false, violating R3. Cover both directions and ensure unsupported local association syntax cannot prove absence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N51\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\",\n      \"line\": 35,\n      \"summary\": \"Handle escaped angle brackets inside angle-bracket destinations without silently dropping the link. For '[decision](<../adr/decision.md#f\\\\> with space>)', CommonMark resolves the destination to decision.md with a fragment, but the extracted production expressions return no destinations. The angle branch stops at the escaped '>', while the bare branch cannot consume the spaces. '[program](<../roadmaps/pair.md#f\\\\> with space>)' fails identically in the reverse direction. No undecodable diagnostic is generated, so a two-member roadmap with only this association receives a known exemption. Parse the complete destination or fail closed and add forward/backward regression cases.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N52\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\",\n      \"line\": 56,\n      \"summary\": \"Preserve backslash-escaped ampersands while decoding character references. CommonMark resolves '[decision](../adr/decision\\\\&num;name.md)' to '../adr/decision&num;name.md', a permitted ADR basename. The implementation first applies html.UnescapeString, turning '&num;' into '#', then removes the backslash and strips the supposed fragment. A read-only decoding probe confirmed that the production path becomes '../adr/decision'; the extension predicate silently skips it. With that regular ADR present and no other association, the result is a known exemption rather than required review. Decode Markdown escapes and entities with their actual precedence, and cover escaped entity introducers. This is an unresolved part of R14-N48.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N53\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\",\n      \"line\": 45,\n      \"summary\": \"The existing F6 residual risk remains: links in code/comments count as associations, and destinations containing parentheses can become unknown. This conservatively requires extra review and does not itself grant an exemption. Inspection and the independently passing RoundTwelve/RoundFourteen regressions support retaining this limited over-enforcement risk.\",\n      \"action\": \"Complete spec follow-up F6 with context-aware Markdown parsing while preserving fail-closed handling of unsupported local associations.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-13\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N48\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The exact percent-escape and character-reference examples now normalize correctly at closeout_adr_associations.go:50-65; TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundFifteen passed in the independently executed three-package test run. However, line 56 still decodes backslash-escaped entity introducers incorrectly. The read-only CommonMark/production-decoding probe for decision\\\\&num;name.md demonstrates the remaining silent exemption described in N52.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N49\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"closeout_adr_associations.go:45-47 deliberately reads code/comments as prose, and lines 191-193 and 266-268 conservatively reject parentheses. RoundTwelve and RoundFourteen regressions passed. Existing spec follow-up F6 remains applicable and is retained as accepted low risk N53.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed R1-R7, D1/D2, the accepted closeout ADR, the bounded-read ADR amendment, declared production changes, schemas, templates, manuals and scaffold copies. Traced CLI close and recovery, closeout-check, review-check, review verification, review-plan, attention/obligations, reached, nextCloses, roadmap gates, MCP closeout state, federated acceptance, readiness, portfolio projection and doctor through the shared decision and terminal projections. Checked recorded-review vetoes under never, always against singleton inheritance and unreviewed_milestones, mandatory-human and baseline protection, canonical members/transfers, unknown associations, receipt immutability, intent/status/receipt sequencing, historical closure, install/update/adopt/setup and schema preservation. Independently ran closeout-policy tests across pose/cli/mcpserver and go vet; compared production Markdown extraction and decoding against CommonMark for forward and reverse forms. Inspected sealed strict validation: 213 checks passed. Ran required artifact/surface commands and suggest-review. No further established blocker was found outside N50-N52; no repository changes or attestation were made.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Distinguished independently verified code/tests from the sealed full-validation run. The original N48 examples pass, but escaped entity introducers remain unresolved. F6 is accepted only for conservative over-enforcement. Global remote backlink discovery and nonparticipating external writers remain outside the accepted design. Artifact-command limitations are disclosed rather than treated as proof of current-range reconciliation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected guarded authorization rechecks, ExpectAbsent receipt publication and intent/status/receipt sequencing. Existing coordination and bounded read-view mechanisms remain in use; interrupted publication stays incomplete and existing receipts are not overwritten.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Schema 5 explicitly migrates policy semantics, schemas 1-4 preserve legacy behavior, CLI configuration writes the pair together, and MCP additions remain projections. Reviewed receipt and review-plan schema additions and transport parity tests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N50\",\n      \"rationale\": \"N50-N52 show supported association inputs becoming silent absence rather than resolved associations or actionable unknown diagnostics.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Traced shared domain evaluation through CLI/MCP, receipt-backed producer proof, canonical transfer targets and aggregate dependency closure. The established parser defects affect the common domain result rather than creating transport-specific behavior.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N50\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Missed reference definitions produce no unknown-association diagnostic, concealing why review was incorrectly exempted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-policy-adoption-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected explicit adoption, update preservation, legacy sealed-plan recognition, reference/transfer toggles and previous-release tests. Older engines intentionally refuse newly adopted schema-5 instances; existing legacy instances are not silently adopted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N51\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Valid local Markdown associations can disappear and incorrectly exempt aggregate review; N50 and N52 establish additional cases.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 separates explicit closure from independent review using deterministic thresholds. D2 reuses the resolver and adoption surfaces and adds receipts because milestone close previously lacked a persisted transition. Shared evaluation addresses inconsistent projections; the remaining defects concern association recognition within that design.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-3ce6ee69\",\n          \"basis\": \"R4\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The spec's implementation reconciliation links explicit-close delivery to the measured read-budget refusal. The ADR amendment documents the bounded increase to 1 GiB and the separate digest-only follow-up.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-c74440ab\",\n          \"basis\": \"R3\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The roadmap template exposes adrs: [] for the explicit associations used by the when-justified rule.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-ec2d86f4\",\n          \"basis\": \"R1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The accepted ADR records policy location, deterministic modes, defaults, historical compatibility and authority protections.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared English/Portuguese manuals, scaffold copies and roadmap templates with policy names, thresholds, adoption, explicit close and receipt behavior. The documented association contract is clear; N50-N52 are implementation failures against it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N50\",\n      \"rationale\": \"An operator receives a known exemption without the missing-association explanation needed to correct the input or require review.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N50\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R3 is not fully satisfied: explicit reference-style associations can be lost. N51-N52 establish further R3 failures despite the passing registered suite.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared declared artifacts and implementation with R1-R7 and D1/D2. Policy, receipts, reader integration, setup/doctor and documentation support aggregate closeout. The bounded-read change is explicitly reconciled in the spec. No global ADR identity framework or MCP configuration/write tool was introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N52\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Incorrect destination decoding can weaken the review authority gate by interpreting a real association as absent.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A shared evaluator and immutable terminal receipt are proportionate to separating review from close. Reusing adopt/setup and the resolver avoids unnecessary new frameworks. Metadata alone would lose existing Markdown associations. A narrow extractor is sufficient only if unsupported local forms fail closed; N50-N52 identify violations requiring correction. Remote backlink inventory remains deliberately excluded.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran the exact command; exit 0. Output included artifact.claims=46, artifact.observed=195 and artifact.findings=920, with provenance warnings. It reported recorded change set cs-b4c4da227b9c ending at 9b8eb4c0, so this is a successful command exit, not proof of warning-free reconciliation of the sealed range. An additional --from/--to invocation failed with 'git diff failed: signal: broken pipe'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Did not run an assessment writer under the read-only boundary. Examined the spec, ADRs, code and sealed structure:design-584572eae6be33ac, and supplied all structural mappings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Did not regenerate assessment artifacts. Inspected component sources, validation registration and sealed pose-mcp evidence directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Did not run the assessment writer. Traced CLI/MCP/federation integration and inspected sealed integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration; independently reran the three-package policy tests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Did not write assessment artifacts. Inspected changed production markers and explicit spec follow-ups, including F5 bounded-read capacity debt and F6 parser over-enforcement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion gate depends on POSE recording and verifying this review conclusion; no attestation was recorded by this review.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion gate must follow the recorded review conclusion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Exit 0; selected backend-go, security and documentation-style under the review workflow. Also applied delivery-evidence and consulted knowledge governance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran pose surface-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict; exit 0 with surface.targets=1, surface.results=213 and surface.findings=0. Composition evidence: integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration. Reachability evidence: reachability:pose-mcp/go/closeout-plan-reachability. This does not cover the newly established parser cases.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Disposed from the sealed strict producer run as requested. Inspected delivery-validation.json: 213 executed, 213 passed, zero failed/errored/skipped. Did not rerun the repository-writing validation producer. Independently executed go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver -run TestCloseoutReviewPolicy -count=1; all three packages passed. go vet ./... also passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The sealed strict run supplies the component's registered build, unit, integration and e2e evidence. Current targeted domain/CLI/MCP tests and go vet passed independently. Passing checks do not resolve the uncovered R3 cases N50-N52.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
